<div class="inner_cell">
<div class="text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<p>The analysis showed that bike share usage followed similar daily patterns across all three cities, with ridership increasing during the morning and reaching another peak in the late afternoon. Washington recorded the highest number of rides overall and showed pronounced morning and evening commuting patterns. New York City experienced its highest ridership during the late afternoon, while Chicago also peaked around 5:00 PM. Across all three cities, bike usage was lowest during the overnight hours, suggesting that demand is largely driven by commuting and daytime travel.</p>

</div>
</div>
