<div class="cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered"><div class="prompt input_prompt">
</div>
<div class="inner_cell">
<div class="text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<p>he analysis identified the most frequently used bike share start stations in each city. In Chicago, Streeter Dr &amp; Grand Ave was the busiest start station. In New York City, Pershing Square North recorded the highest number of departures, and in Washington, D.C., Columbus Circle / Union Station was the most frequently used starting location. These results suggest that riders tend to begin trips at stations located near major business districts, transportation hubs, and popular destinations, highlighting the importance of these locations within each city's bike share network.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered"><div class="prompt input_prompt">
</div>
<div class="inner_cell">
<div class="text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<h3 id="Question-3">Question 3<a class="anchor-link" href="#Question-3">&#182;</a></h3><p>How do bike share user types differ among Chicago, New York City, and Washington, D.C.?</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="cell border-box-sizing code_cell rendered">
<div class="input">
<div class="prompt input_prompt">In&nbsp;[16]:</div>
<div class="inner_cell">
    <div class="input_area">
<div class=" highlight hl-r"><pre><span></span><span class="c1"># Count user types for each city</span>
<span class="n">user_types</span> <span class="o">&lt;-</span> <span class="nf">rbind</span><span class="p">(</span>
    <span class="nf">data.frame</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">City</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="s">&quot;Chicago&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span>
               <span class="n">User.Type</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="nf">names</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="nf">table</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">chi</span><span class="o">$</span><span class="n">User.Type</span><span class="p">)),</span>
               <span class="n">Count</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="nf">as.numeric</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="nf">table</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">chi</span><span class="o">$</span><span class="n">User.Type</span><span class="p">))),</span>
    
    <span class="nf">data.frame</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">City</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="s">&quot;New York City&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span>
               <span class="n">User.Type</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="nf">names</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="nf">table</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">ny</span><span class="o">$</span><span class="n">User.Type</span><span class="p">)),</span>
               <span class="n">Count</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="nf">as.numeric</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="nf">table</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">ny</span><span class="o">$</span><span class="n">User.Type</span><span class="p">))),</span>
    
    <span class="nf">data.frame</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">City</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="s">&quot;Washington&quot;</span><span class="p">,</span>
               <span class="n">User.Type</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="nf">names</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="nf">table</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">wash</span><span class="o">$</span><span class="n">User.Type</span><span class="p">)),</span>
               <span class="n">Count</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="nf">as.numeric</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="nf">table</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">wash</span><span class="o">$</span><span class="n">User.Type</span><span class="p">)))</span>
<span class="p">)</span>

<span class="n">user_types</span>
</pre></div>

</div>
</div>
</div>

