<p>The comparison of user types showed that subscribers made up the majority of bike share users in all three cities. Washington recorded the largest number of both subscribers and customers, followed by New York City and Chicago. In each city, subscriber memberships greatly outnumbered customer rides, suggesting that many users rely on the bike share system for regular transportation rather than occasional use. These results indicate that recurring memberships play an important role in supporting bike share programs across the three cities.</p>

